# Keep Both Lockfiles in Sync

This repo commits two lockfiles and both are load-bearing:

| Lockfile | Used by |
|----------|---------|
| `bun.lock` | Local development (`bun install`, `bun run …`) |
| `package-lock.json` | Vercel builds (`npm install`, chosen because the file exists) |

If `package.json` gains a dependency that `package-lock.json` doesn't pin,
Vercel resolves it fresh from the public registry on every build. A new
upstream release can then break the deploy with no change in this repo (e.g.
`npm error code ERESOLVE`).

## Rules

- **Any change to `dependencies` or `devDependencies` in `package.json` must
  update `bun.lock` and `package-lock.json` in the same commit.** Follow the
  [`update-lockfiles` skill](../skills/update-lockfiles/SKILL.md).
- Never delete or stop updating either lockfile.
- Before opening a PR that touches `package.json` or a lockfile, both must
  pass:
  - `npm ls --package-lock-only` (package-lock.json matches package.json)
  - `bun run strip-lock-proxy:check` (no proxy URLs — see
    [`bun-clean-lock-rule.mdc`](bun-clean-lock-rule.mdc))
- Do not hand-edit lockfiles beyond what `scripts/strip-bun-lock-proxy.ts`
  does.

The pre-commit hook in `.githooks/pre-commit` enforces the `npm ls` check
whenever `package.json` or `package-lock.json` is staged.
